Please note that this code assumes a Unix-like environment and uses the `rand()` function to generate random CRC flags. In a real-world scenario, you would likely want to use a more robust random number generator and handle errors more thoroughly.

```java
public MoSTState fetchAndProcessState(String filePath) throws DFSClientNotAvailableException, NetworkConnectivityException, ClassLoadingException {
    try (ObjectInputStream ois = new DFSClient().getObjectInputStream(filePath)) {
        Object obj = ois.readObject();
        if (obj instanceof MoSTState) {
            return (MoSTState) obj;
        } else {
            return null;
        }
    } catch (EOFException e) {
        throw new NetworkConnectivityException("Error reading file", e);
    } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
        throw new ClassLoadingException("Error loading object", e);
    } catch (SecurityException e) {
        throw new DFSClientNotAvailableException("DFS client unavailable", e);
    }
}
